  "root_cause": {
    "text": "The IPv4/IPv6 UDP datagram append paths failed to mark spliced page fragments with the `SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG` flag, causing the ESP input handler to incorrectly assume private ownership of shared pipe pages and perform unsafe in-place decryption.",
    "evidence": "The CVE description states \"The IPv4/IPv6 datagram append paths did not set this flag when splicing pages into UDP skbs,\" leading to ESP taking the \"no-COW fast path for uncloned skbs without a frag_list and decrypts in place over data that is not owned privately by the skb.\" The patch fixes this by adding `skb_shinfo(skb)->flags |= SKBFL_SHARED_FRAG;` in `net/ipv4/ip_output.c` and `net/ipv6/ip6_output.c`, and updating `net/ipv4/esp4.c` and `net/ipv6/esp6.c` to check `!skb_has_shared_frag(skb)` before skipping the copy-on-write operation.",
    "passed_review": true
  },
  "vuln_statements": [
